MID_EV20_008_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_008_m01_001: Divine Emperor! I have urgent news.
MID_EV20_008_m01_002: General Lind's advance has been repelled at the\nplains of Klytius.
MID_EV20_008_m01_003: I don't believe what I'm hearing. That shouldn't\nhave been possible!
MID_EV20_008_m01_004: Between our armies and the forces of our vassal\nstates, did we not send a hundred thousand men?
MID_EV20_008_m01_005: Yes...but the reports say Brezarant betrayed us to\nside with Saramis.
MID_EV20_008_m01_006: Our forces were routed. General Lind is currently\nregrouping at Agris Stronghold.
MID_EV20_008_m01_007: Meanwhile, the Saramis-Brezarant Alliance is\nmarching north up the Agris Thoroughfare.
MID_EV20_008_m01_008: What?! So...that's what Mars was scheming.\nThat bastard.
MID_EV20_008_m01_009: Summon the high priest of Mars's temple right now.\nAnd get me Mars as well!
MID_EV20_008_m01_010: W-well...Mars's temple has closed its gates. It looks\nlike they intend to resist until the bitter end.
MID_EV20_008_m01_011: Deploy the vulkans to break them. Take everyone\nstill inside that temple prisoner!
MID_EV20_008_m01_012: Hmph. Not only do I need to wipe Saramis off the\nmap, now I have to crush Brezarant too.
MID_EV20_008_m01_013: But...we're talking about Mars, the Bringer of War.\nI'm not sure we can win.
MID_EV20_008_m01_014: I'll lead the charge myself if I have to. Damn every\none of them for defying me.
MID_EV20_008_m01_015: Maybe a show of force will keep them from getting\nany big ideas.
MID_EV20_008_m01_016: Pardon the intrusion, Emperor. The work of restoring\nyour cauldron is now complete.
MID_EV20_008_m01_017: Finally, some good news. Well done, Raksha.
MID_EV20_008_m01_018: I could down a tub's worth of flamma. Maybe that's\nwhat I need to clear this foul—
MID_EV20_008_m01_019: *yawn* I wake for the first time in ages and find\neverything in a tizzy. What's all this commotion?
MID_EV20_008_m01_020: A-ah— Fortuna? Is that you?
MID_EV20_008_m01_021: Well! Now this is a surprise. Where have you been\nhiding all this time?
MID_EV20_008_m01_022: And I cannot seem to find Solel anywhere. Where\nhas he gone?
MID_EV20_008_m01_023: W-well...you see...
MID_EV20_008_m01_024: Hmm.
MID_EV20_008_m01_025: Causality swirls about you like a terrible storm.\nJust what have you set in motion?
MID_EV20_008_m01_026: Nothing, I... I am simply carrying out the duties\nI was given.
MID_EV20_008_m01_027: Worse, the chaos of this causality seems to stretch\ninfinitely into the future.
MID_EV20_008_m01_028: I've rarely seen its like. We are on the precipice of\na truly extraordinary event.
MID_EV20_008_m01_029: Damned fool. You've just awoken and you're already\nstarting this.
MID_EV20_008_m01_030: Do you lack the imagination to consider that a\nsleeping dog, once roused, may bite?
MID_EV20_008_m01_031: If this continues, I've no doubt you shall find yourself\nin a havoc far beyond your control.
MID_EV20_008_m01_032: You should not speak to your father the Divine\nEmperor in that way.
MID_EV20_008_m01_033: This rudeness has crossed a line.
MID_EV20_008_m01_034: Heh. You. I've always found it curious, you know.
MID_EV20_008_m01_035: You are as inscrutable as one obscured behind\na curtain.
MID_EV20_008_m01_036: I have no sense of your past, nor your heart, nor the\ncausality I ought to spy in your future.
MID_EV20_008_m01_037: Odd, for the eyes of the Goddess of Fate.
MID_EV20_008_m01_038: Wouldn't you agree? Do you know what I think of\none whose mind is so thoroughly shrouded?
MID_EV20_008_m01_039: 'Tis a proclamation to all the world that you are\nsomeone of consequence. But who?
MID_EV20_008_m01_040: That is some flight of fancy. I am the Divine\nEmperor's faithful servant, nothing more.
MID_EV20_008_m01_041: As you please. But hold your tongue, for I have more\nto say to this fool.
MID_EV20_008_m01_042: I suspect that she may look unfavorably on your\nactions since waking.
MID_EV20_008_m01_043: As you might guess from my own displeasure.
MID_EV20_008_m01_044: No... I was only following Mother's orders!
MID_EV20_008_m01_045: She told me to use all the strength at my disposal to\nrule this land, and so I am.
MID_EV20_008_m01_046: Then you'd swear on her name that you're not doing\nanything you know you shouldn't?
MID_EV20_008_m01_047: Yes... Yes, of course. I swear it by the name of\nthe progenitor god.
MID_EV20_008_m01_048: Very well, then. I didn't come to pry into your affairs.
MID_EV20_008_m01_049: 'Tis simply my own duty to bear witness to\neverything that happens in this land.
MID_EV20_008_m01_050: And to convey these things to her.
MID_EV20_008_m01_051: Now, if you ever did go too far, she might decide to\ndeclare a verdict through me.
MID_EV20_008_m01_052: So I would be very careful if I were you. Consider\nthat your warning.
MID_EV20_008_m01_053: I shall be away from Dagsion for a time. I have\nspecial business to attend to.
MID_EV20_008_m01_054: Divine Emperor...was it wise to allow Fortuna\nto leave?
MID_EV20_008_m01_055: Never mind. Under no circumstances will we act\nagainst that one.
MID_EV20_008_m01_056: But surely Fortuna showed too much disrespect as\none of your children.
MID_EV20_008_m01_057: I said we will not act against her!
MID_EV20_008_m01_058: I beg your forgiveness. I spoke out of turn.
MID_EV20_008_m01_059: Listen to me. You must not even lay a finger on her.\nShe is special among my daughters.
MID_EV20_008_m01_060: That's if she even counts as a "daughter."\nHonestly, she's...{SetColor=Gray}nothing but a monster...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV20_008_m01_061: Pardon? What was that, Divine Emperor?
MID_EV20_008_m01_062: {SetColor=Gray}Rrgh...{SetColor=Default}
MID_NR20_02_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_02_m01_001: Dagda's cauldron had been hidden under the capital\nfor over 450 years—the accursed site almost lost to\nhistory. But now it again saw the light of day.
MID_NR20_02_m01_002: The arena was gone, and with it, all traces of the\ntales brought to life with battles and bravery.\nWhat people saw in its place was like a portal\nto the underworld.
MID_NR20_02_m01_003: The public gathered for a dread spectacle—prisoners\nthrown into the cauldron, where they melted away,\nscreaming, all by order of the Divine Emperor.
MID_NR20_02_m01_004: Legends resurfaced with fresh horror. Long ago, the\ncauldron had claimed many lives—tens of thousands.\nDagsion's citizens feared far darker times to come.
MID_NR20_02_m01_005: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 2, Chapter 1
MID_EV20_009_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_009_m01_001: P-please, no! If you take that, my family won't\nhave enough to eat!
MID_EV20_009_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_009_m01_002: You can't! That's all our savings!
MID_EV20_009_m01_003: Theodora! Your soldiers are raiding the town. Tell\nthem to stop!
MID_EV20_009_m01_004: That would be foolish. The warriors of Saramis are\nnot doing this to line their own pockets.
MID_EV20_009_m01_005: All supplies collected by the cavalry will be used\nsolely for our army's upkeep.
MID_EV20_009_m01_006: You ordered them to do this?!
MID_EV20_009_m01_007: Of course. Our forces have swelled to a hundred\nthousand—well beyond what we can support.
MID_EV20_009_m01_008: War is an ugly business. A deficit of supplies would\ncause morale to suffer significantly.
MID_EV20_009_m01_009: Besides, we are in enemy territory. What reason have\nwe for restraint?
MID_EV20_009_m01_010: Whatever you need, you can draw from my\nkingdom's treasury.
MID_EV20_009_m01_011: Agree to stop this pillaging, and you may buy\nyour supplies on Brezarant's tab.
MID_EV20_009_m01_012: Do you grasp how much money is required to\nmaintain an army of this size?
MID_EV20_009_m01_013: Gaitz. How much do you think we can we afford?
MID_EV20_009_m01_014: Well...in terms of what's immediately accessible,\naround 20 million gold.
MID_EV20_009_m01_015: But if we spend all that, we will be taking on\nsome debt...
MID_EV20_009_m01_016: Fine. When the war's over, we can turn our swords\nto plowshares.
MID_EV20_009_m01_017: This makes no sense. Why would you go to such\nlengths for enemy civilians?
MID_EV20_009_m01_018: Because I know the despair of having everything\nstripped away.
MID_EV20_009_m01_019: How it feels to watch a happy, carefree life get burnt\nto cinders.
MID_EV20_009_m01_020: And? It is enough for me that Saramis prospers.
MID_EV20_009_m01_021: It shouldn't be. We're not going to end the suffering if\nour vision stops at our countries' borders.
MID_EV20_009_m01_022: Rob the parents, and the children grow up to curse\nyour name.
MID_EV20_009_m01_023: You think they'll run gladly into our new alliance just\nbecause Dagda is gone?
MID_EV20_009_m01_024: I wish I could convey to you how naïve you sound.
MID_EV20_009_m01_025: Can't you see? This is why I fight, Theodora.
MID_EV20_009_m01_026: I know I'm draining Brezarant's coffers.
MID_EV20_009_m01_027: But my kingdom's riches are a modest price to pay\nfor the trust we'd lose.
MID_EV20_009_m01_028: Mm...
MID_EV20_009_m01_029: You are still naïve—but your naïveté is growing on\nme. Very well. I shall assent to this plan.
MID_EV20_009_m01_030: Bonaventure! Recall the cavalry at once.
MID_EV20_009_m01_031: And send a messenger to our homeland with orders\nto convey provisions and funds to the front line.
MID_EV20_009_m01_032: Until they arrive, negotiate with local merchants for\nsupplies, paid for with whatever is on hand.
MID_EV20_009_m01_033: At once. But we are already far from Saramis.\nThe convoys will take time.
MID_EV20_009_m01_034: Moreover, we must leave some of our reserves\nthere to deal with the Mosa.
MID_EV20_009_m01_035: Even with the funds from Brezarant, we cannot\nmaintain our situation indefinitely.
MID_EV20_009_m01_036: How long do you estimate we can hold out?
MID_EV20_009_m01_037: As things stand? Something like two months.
MID_EV20_009_m01_038: Hm.
MID_EV20_009_m01_039: A nice quagmire I landed you in.
MID_EV20_009_m01_040: None of that. You were right. Besides, I never go\nback on my word once given.
MID_EV20_009_m01_041: But we have little margin for error now. Our enemy\noutnumbers us tremendously.
MID_EV20_009_m01_042: We must act as if we walk a razor's edge.
MID_EV20_009_m01_043: If we can take Agris Stronghold, which lies before\nus, we may be able to seize their stockpiled supplies.
MID_EV20_009_m01_044: Which would allow us to survive a bit longer.\nSo long as they do not set fire to the provisions...
MID_EV20_009_m01_045: Then again...there is another card I may yet play.
MID_EV20_009_m01_046: Our King Bertrand is cut from different cloth,\nit would seem.
MID_EV20_009_m01_047: As queen of Saramis, I have been single-minded in\nensuring that my own people thrive.
MID_EV20_009_m01_048: Yet I see a grander purpose in his eyes.
MID_EV20_009_m01_049: Is it folly? Or the philosophy of a true monarch?
MID_EV20_009_m01_050: If it is the latter, then this war will be the test.
MID_EV20_100_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_100_m01_001: Hey. You called? I heard you had something serious\nto talk about.
MID_EV20_100_m01_002: You arrived quickly. Thank you for that.
MID_EV20_100_m01_003: Showing up when you're needed is the hallmark of\na great merchant.
MID_EV20_100_m01_005: Do you recall the wager we once made?
MID_EV20_100_m01_006: Ah... How could I forget? The time has come to call\nthat in, has it?
MID_EV20_100_m01_007: With Saramis's back against the wall, I imagine you'll\nneed all the help you can get.
MID_EV20_100_m01_008: You read the situation accurately. We need you.
MID_EV20_100_m01_009: Fair enough. A promise is a promise, after all.\nHow much do you need?
MID_EV20_100_m01_010: Hm. For now, something in the realm of 30 million\ngold would ease our immediate concerns.
MID_EV20_100_m01_011: *whistle* That's a tall order.
MID_EV20_100_m01_012: Clearing this with Ursula is going to be...so much fun.
MID_EV20_100_m01_013: As I said then, whatever I borrow shall be repaid.\nSo long as Saramis still stands at the end of it.
MID_EV20_100_m01_014: Frankly, it's a bit much, especially with the Grania\ncanal plan in the works... But I did promise.
MID_EV20_100_m01_015: If we can, I'd like to avoid getting even further on\nthe empire's bad side.
MID_EV20_100_m01_016: So try to keep the Vandahl Trading Company's\ninvolvement a secret.
MID_EV20_100_m01_017: Worry not on that score. We have no relations with\nthe empire for the moment.
MID_EV20_100_m01_018: Thirty million... I had a feeling you'd be turning my\npocketbook inside out.
MID_EV20_100_m01_019: But say no more, Majesty! I'll see it done.
MID_EV20_100_m01_020: You seem to me to be enjoying the moment\ndespite yourself.
MID_EV20_100_m01_021: Well. You've given me a front-row seat to history in\nthe making.
MID_EV20_100_m01_022: With a merchant's heart like mine, what more could\nI possibly ask for?
MID_NR20_03_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_03_m01_001: Dagdan Imperial Calendar, year 1450, Febrai.
MID_NR20_03_m01_002: The Alliance left the Klytius plains after defeating\nthe empire's army, and then marched on Amalthea,\nwith Saramis and Brezarant standing firm together.
MID_NR20_03_m01_003: They came to Agris Stronghold at the border. There,\nafter the loss to the Alliance, Lind had regathered\nhis forces, well-fortified for the upcoming battle.
MID_NR20_03_m01_004: The stronghold was thought beyond capture.
MID_NR20_03_m01_005: Theodora's bold march toward Dagsion had come to\na complete halt. She and her allies now stared up\nat a fortress of imposing proportions.
MID_NR20_03_m01_006: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 2, Chapter 4
MID_EV20_010_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_010_m01_001: Agris Stronghold is a fortress at a strategic point on\nthe Agris Thoroughfare in the Karoli Wilderness.
MID_EV20_010_m01_002: The Dagdan Empire has combined its own forces\nwith the kingdom of Arago.
MID_EV20_010_m01_003: They are stationed at this fortress in a position of\nstrength against us.
MID_EV20_010_m01_094: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_095: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_096: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_097: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_098: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_099: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_100: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_101: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_102: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_103: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_104: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_105: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_106: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_107: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_108: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_109: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_110: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_111: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_112: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_113: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_004: Huh. I hadn't really thought about it before, but \nseeing it like this... It looks like a huge fortress.
MID_EV20_010_m01_007: How are we supposed to attack something like this?\nFeels impossible, doesn't it?
MID_EV20_010_m01_008: We've got the forces and the momentum right now,\nso it'll be a head-on assault without a lot of tricks.
MID_EV20_010_m01_009: If we get past here, Dagsion will be just a stone's\nthrow away.
MID_EV20_010_m01_010: We've come so far. There's no turning back now.
MID_EV20_010_m01_011: Honestly, there's a lot I'm worried about. But none of\nit really matters until we win.
MID_EV20_010_m01_012: There's one way forward, and I need to be at\nmy best.
MID_EV20_010_m01_013: It is a formidable fortress and has stood for a\nlong time.
MID_EV20_010_m01_014: You won't find many as old as this one in Fódlan.
MID_EV20_010_m01_015: It is no surprise you marvel at it.
MID_EV20_010_m01_016: You seem happy, Sweetie.
MID_EV20_010_m01_017: When I stand at the edge of the battlefield, my\nchest begins to throb with anticipation.
MID_EV20_010_m01_018: Yeah, that's not a thing that happens to me.
MID_EV20_010_m01_019: This fortress was built on the border between\nAmalthea, where Dagsion is, and Melias.
MID_EV20_010_m01_020: If we make it through here, we'll be on the doorstep\nof Dagsion.
MID_EV20_010_m01_021: Perhaps this battle will grant me the pleasure I seek.
MID_EV20_010_m01_022: For now, I long to hear the cries that mark the start\nof the fray.
MID_EV20_010_m01_023: Yech. Now that I get a look at it, it's a lot bigger\nthan your average stronghold.
MID_EV20_010_m01_024: Gonna be a tough nut to crack. I kinda wish I was\nanywhere else right now.
MID_EV20_010_m01_025: Hm! This garrison is remarkably large, even among\nthe many strongholds of Dagda.
MID_EV20_010_m01_026: Boss, why would they build a big fortress like that\nsmack in the middle of the road?
MID_EV20_010_m01_027: It may have been meant to guard against incursions\nfrom the south...such as ours.
MID_EV20_010_m01_028: But recall that it was Fort Zanbar's position in the\nmountains that made it nearly impregnable.
MID_EV20_010_m01_029: A fortress situated here is nothing more to us than\na larger-than-usual obstacle.
MID_EV20_010_m01_030: Let us show its inhabitants the Saramis way.
MID_EV20_010_m01_031: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_032: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_033: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_034: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_035: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_036: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_037: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_038: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_039: It won't be easy to punch through the fortress's\ndefenses.
MID_EV20_010_m01_040: I wonder why they saw the need to build this\nimposing citadel here.
MID_EV20_010_m01_041: Likely in order to defend Amalthea, the region that\ncontains Dagsion.
MID_EV20_010_m01_042: Why is it so close to the capital, and not somewhere\nfarther out?
MID_EV20_010_m01_043: I suspect Dagda the Great feared an invasion from\nthe southerners.
MID_EV20_010_m01_044: While outwardly he treated them as his vassals,\nperhaps he never trusted them.
MID_EV20_010_m01_045: That's kind of sad. He thought he needed defending\nfrom people in his own continent?
MID_EV20_010_m01_046: And he wasn't entirely wrong. We're here, after all—\nwith that thing blocking our way.
MID_EV20_010_m01_047: Tsk... We're wasting time.
MID_EV20_010_m01_048: The longer this war goes on, the longer I'm waiting\nto kill him.
MID_EV20_010_m01_049: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_050: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_052: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_053: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_054: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_055: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_056: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_057: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_058: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_059: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_060: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_061: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_062: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_063: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_064: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_065: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_066: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_067: 
MID_EV20_010_m01_068: Sorry to interrupt, Theodora. My congratulations on\nyour victory at Klytius.
MID_EV20_010_m01_069: Troy! It is a balm to have you with us.
MID_EV20_010_m01_070: I was recently divining your fortune. The hexagram\nwas...disconcerting.
MID_EV20_010_m01_071: Ah, is this the same divination method you often\nused to counsel my father?
MID_EV20_010_m01_072: Which hexagram has you so concerned?
MID_EV20_010_m01_073: Jian, or "hardship." One of the four hexagrams of\ndifficulty. It represents challenging circumstances.
MID_EV20_010_m01_074: And sure enough, there's trouble in the northeast.\nThe road to Dagsion will not be straightforward.
MID_EV20_010_m01_075: The reading cautions against action. But you cannot\nafford to remain idle, can you?
MID_EV20_010_m01_076: We cannot. A battle of attrition is one we will lose.
MID_EV20_010_m01_077: I am sorry to disregard your advice, Auntie, but we\nmust proceed.
MID_EV20_010_m01_078: That's alright. I came with a backup plan.
MID_EV20_010_m01_079: You know, Anatolia once gave me a dismal reading\nin Dagsion.
MID_EV20_010_m01_080: Ever since, I have put no stock in fortune-telling.\nI only want to know if the hexagram is favorable.
MID_EV20_010_m01_081: The divination we Mediators employ enhances the\nprinciples of Bagua with magic.
MID_EV20_010_m01_082: It's far more accurate than your average street\nmystic. Don't take it lightly.
MID_EV20_010_m01_083: What do you think of our chances in today's battle?
MID_EV20_010_m01_084: Morale is high and justice is on our side. So long as\nwe face ordinary humans, we shall not falter.
MID_EV20_010_m01_085: I agree with your conclusion, so long as the\npremise holds.
MID_EV20_010_m01_086: You know more than you let on. What is it?
MID_EV20_010_m01_087: When you're going up against Dagda the Great, no\namount of preparation is too much.
MID_EV20_010_m01_088: Which reminds me, I've heard odd things from my\ncontacts in Dagsion.
MID_EV20_010_m01_089: They say that Dagda's cauldron has been unearthed\nin the plaza there.
MID_EV20_010_m01_090: What?! The one that claimed so many lives?\nYou mean to say it still exists?
MID_EV20_010_m01_091: I thought the colosseum served as a lid covering\nDagda's cauldron.
MID_EV20_010_m01_092: It did. But I'm told the colosseum was demolished,\nexposing the cauldron directly below.
MID_EV20_010_m01_093: What could Dagda be planning by reopening it?
MID_EV20_011_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_011_m01_001: That's odd. Look, my hands are shaking.
MID_EV20_011_m01_002: You're right. That is strange. I've never known you\nto have shaky hands.
MID_EV20_011_m01_003: Yet I don't feel afraid. It must be that I'm trembling\nwith excitement for the battle to come.
MID_EV20_011_m01_004: Odder still is that... Well, you know me. I take a\ncynic's view of most things.
MID_EV20_011_m01_005: Yet here I find myself sincerely bent on settling the\nscore with Bertrand and his new allies.
MID_EV20_011_m01_006: Heh. I don't know what's come over me.
MID_EV20_011_m01_007: You and I have seen a lot of battles. But I can't\nremember you ever getting like this before one.
MID_EV20_011_m01_008: We're in a tough spot. I felt this at Klytius too.
MID_EV20_011_m01_009: They're fighting to save their whole world, while\nwe're fighting for...nothing, really.
MID_EV20_011_m01_010: Theodora and Bertrand, huh. I bet the soldiers\nthey're leading don't have these doubts.
MID_EV20_011_m01_011: I wouldn't say we fight for nothing. Our cause is\nthe will of the Divine Emperor.
MID_EV20_011_m01_012: Don't put up that front. I doubt it's how you\nreally feel.
MID_EV20_011_m01_013: True enough. But the fact remains—the prospect of\nthis fight excites me.
MID_EV20_011_m01_014: If we lose here, Nathan, I hope you abandon this\ndamned cause of ours.
MID_EV20_011_m01_015: Make your escape, even if you must dirty your hands,\nand return to Arago as a loyal soldier.
MID_EV20_011_m01_016: I've long thought King Gilchris to be a fool, unworthy\nof his station.
MID_EV20_011_m01_017: But I guess you need somewhere to point that\nunbending loyalty of yours.
MID_EV20_011_m01_018: Stop this talk. When I return home, it will be with\nyou. Any other way would be wrong.
MID_EV20_011_m01_019: Hmph. Fleeing the scene with the dirt of defeat\nunder my nails isn't my style.
MID_EV20_011_m01_020: Creek...you don't plan on dying here, do you?
MID_EV20_011_m01_021: I don't have a death wish in me, no.
MID_EV20_011_m01_022: Pardon my brooding. The point is, we need to win\ntoday. Let's both do what we can to accomplish that.
MID_EV20_011_m01_023: Yeah. I'll be sure to watch how you fight when you're\nserious, so I can take notes.
MID_EV20_011_m01_024: The battle will be starting soon. We ought to get to\nour positions.
MID_EV20_011_m01_025: Sure. But I'll say it again—I'm only going back to our\nkingdom with you. So don't get any dumb ideas.
MID_EV20_011_m01_026: I know, I know. Don't fret. I'm just getting it all out\nbefore the big battle.
MID_EV20_011_m01_027: Ah, Nathan. There may be something to your\nsimple, bullheaded way.
MID_EV20_012_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_012_m01_001: Look! The dragon is retreating!
MID_EV20_012_m01_002: The whole imperial army is turning tail and running!
MID_EV20_012_m01_003: We did it... We're saved!
MID_EV20_012_m01_082: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_083: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_084: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_085: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_086: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_087: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_088: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_089: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_090: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_004: Incredible. Who knew Troy had such power at\nher disposal?
MID_EV20_012_m01_005: You have all seen it yourself! Dagda the Great has\ncowered before us!
MID_EV20_012_m01_006: Our victory is no miracle. It is the strength of\nhumanity, granted to us by our distant ancestors!
MID_EV20_012_m01_007: Remember this day, when we showed power and\nrighteousness enough to oppose a god!
MID_EV20_012_m01_008: Reform the battle lines, quickly! And get to work\nrepairing the breaches!
MID_EV20_012_m01_009: We did it! I'm not sure I understand how, but it looks\nlike we won.
MID_EV20_012_m01_010: Oh... I thought we were goners this time.
MID_EV20_012_m01_011: I am...alive right now, right?
MID_EV20_012_m01_012: Driving away a huge dragon... What frightening\npower.
MID_EV20_012_m01_013: If power like that were turned against the temples,\neven the gods wouldn't stand a chance.
MID_EV20_012_m01_014: Is that some type of magic? No, it can't be. That\npower is way beyond the realm of magic.
MID_EV20_012_m01_015: Who could have made such a power? And why?
MID_EV20_012_m01_016: To think a star would fall at her command... Am I to\nbelieve that is the work of human hands?
MID_EV20_012_m01_017: Tell me the truth of it, Fabio, if you know.
MID_EV20_012_m01_018: It was created by humans, yes. I did not think I\nwould see it in this land.
MID_EV20_012_m01_019: To think that they have control of it... No, on\nreflection, it is obvious that they would.
MID_EV20_012_m01_020: This changes the calculus of how Agartha\ncan respond to them.
MID_EV20_012_m01_021: I hope that you people understand the import\nof this.
MID_EV20_012_m01_022: Its use is what triggered the Great Undoing.
MID_EV20_012_m01_023: Now that Dagda has felt its bite...how will\nhe react?
MID_EV20_012_m01_024: I eagerly await his response. This will keep my\nboredom at bay.
MID_EV20_012_m01_025: Wh-what was that?! How were they allowed to\npossess that kind of power?
MID_EV20_012_m01_026: A star, Theodora called it...
MID_EV20_012_m01_027: I'm as stunned as you are. I never imagined the\nkingdom had that kind of strength.
MID_EV20_012_m01_028: Perhaps this is why Dagda was so desperate to\ndestroy the People of the White Egg.
MID_EV20_012_m01_029: Why he perpetrated the Cleansing of Damascar—\nand why he's invading Saramis now.
MID_EV20_012_m01_030: He knew about their power, and he feared it.
MID_EV20_012_m01_031: But if they've had this at their disposal, why are we\nfighting a war at all?
MID_EV20_012_m01_032: I doubt they wanted to rain destruction like that\nupon Dagsion.
MID_EV20_012_m01_033: So it fell to the people to fight. People like us,\nMiss Leda.
MID_EV20_012_m01_034: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_035: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_036: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_037: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_038: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_039: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_040: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_041: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_042: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_043: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_044: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_045: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_046: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_047: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_048: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_049: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_050: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_051: It was a narrow thing, but I made it in time.
MID_EV20_012_m01_052: I am grateful to you, Troy. You have saved us.
MID_EV20_012_m01_053: Think nothing of it. I owed him that much for\nthe past.
MID_EV20_012_m01_054: I'm glad my aim was true this time. Not bad, if I say\nso myself.
MID_EV20_012_m01_055: Dagda the Great won't oppose us so openly now\nthat he knows we have this.
MID_EV20_012_m01_056: I bet he regrets poking the bear about now.
MID_EV20_012_m01_057: What was the nature of that power you used?
MID_EV20_012_m01_058: I recall you once explained it to me by calling it\na star, but...
MID_EV20_012_m01_059: Long, long ago, humans hung it in the sky to use\nagainst other humans.
MID_EV20_012_m01_060: What? The world of the past employed such weapons\nin their wars?
MID_EV20_012_m01_061: Yes. Though they rarely saw use prior to the\nGreat Undoing.
MID_EV20_012_m01_062: No doubt there was an element of deterrence by\nopposing forces keeping each other in check.
MID_EV20_012_m01_063: It's best thought of as a cursed inheritance. I would\nbalk at using it against people.
MID_EV20_012_m01_064: But against Dagda the Great, there is no weapon\nmore suitable.
MID_EV20_012_m01_065: I was never keen on it hanging over all our heads,\nbut today it was a lifesaver. Ironic, isn't it?
MID_EV20_012_m01_066: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_067: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_068: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_069: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_070: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_071: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_072: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_073: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_074: My regrets from that day steeled me to pull the\ntrigger this time.
MID_EV20_012_m01_075: Anatolia, I'm leaving the Artemis controls with you.
MID_EV20_012_m01_076: This power is too great for us. You must choose\ncarefully when to deploy it.
MID_EV20_012_m01_077: 
MID_EV20_012_m01_078: I see...so it was an inheritance from our ancestors\nthat saved us all.
MID_EV20_012_m01_079: Call it what you will, but it's not a good thing.\nDon't forget that.
MID_EV20_012_m01_080: It was weapons like this that set the world on fire\nduring the Great Undoing.
MID_EV20_012_m01_081: In the end, it's only power. All that can keep it on a\nleash is human reason.
MID_EV20_013_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_013_m01_001: No one told me we'd be up against THAT. I didn't\nsign on for this!
MID_EV20_013_m01_002: You there. Just where do you think you're going?
MID_EV20_013_m01_003: Gah! Oh, it's just you. Don't scare me like\nthat, General.
MID_EV20_013_m01_004: Isn't it clear? I'm getting the hell away from\nthis battlefield.
MID_EV20_013_m01_005: You do see why, don't you?
MID_EV20_013_m01_006: A javelin of light from the heavens, piercing a dragon\nblotting out the sky...it's something out of myth.
MID_EV20_013_m01_007: And there's no room in myth for normal humans.\nSo I'm out!
MID_EV20_013_m01_008: When a javelin of light could fall on me any minute,\nrunning is the only sensible plan.
MID_EV20_013_m01_009: But surely you know that desertion from the\nbattlefield is a capital crime.
MID_EV20_013_m01_010: What?! Are you threatening to execute me?
MID_EV20_013_m01_011: D-don't come near me, you damned devil! What if\nI gave you a share of this loot?
MID_EV20_013_m01_012: Your status does you no favors with me. And I won't\nbe bribed, either.
MID_EV20_013_m01_013: Yaaagh!
MID_EV20_013_m01_014: Put this fool's corpse on a stake somewhere\nprominent.
MID_EV20_013_m01_015: Show everyone in the army, no matter their rank,\nwhat'll happen to them if they try to flee.
MID_EV20_013_m01_016: Yes, sir!
MID_EV20_013_m01_017: He had a point, though. Our enemies have a\npractically unbeatable weapon.
MID_EV20_013_m01_018: I didn't think anyone could repel Dagda the Great in\nhis dragon form.
MID_EV20_013_m01_019: Perhaps they've found their own monster to\ncounter ours.
MID_EV20_013_m01_020: This explains a lot about why Dagda the Great was\nso afraid of the People of the White Egg.
MID_EV20_013_m01_021: Hmm.
MID_EV20_013_m01_022: That javelin of light is a problem. But will they be so\neager to deploy it if I use Dagsion as a shield?
MID_EV20_013_m01_023: All I need is a little bit of time to regroup.
MID_EV20_013_m01_024: Very well. We'll leave a fifth of our remaining troops\nhere to harass the Alliance at Agris Stronghold.
MID_EV20_013_m01_025: The rest will retreat to Alcineus Span and build up\nfortifications there.
MID_EV20_013_m01_026: But, General, sir, there's a problem. We don't have\nenough supplies to maintain the army.
MID_EV20_013_m01_027: Why hasn't Dagsion sent more matériel?
MID_EV20_013_m01_028: If that's the only problem, then get pillaging. Take\nwhatever you need from the nearby settlements.
MID_EV20_013_m01_029: You're free to impale any who resist. Then burn\ndown their villages in retaliation. No exceptions.
MID_EV20_013_m01_030: But make sure everything we loot is collected in the\nplaza and accounted for.
MID_EV20_013_m01_031: I want anyone who sneaks a little something for\nthemselves scalped as an example.
MID_EV20_013_m01_032: Oh, and tell the troops there's a reward for\ninforming on disloyalty.
MID_EV20_013_m01_033: B-but, sir...
MID_EV20_013_m01_034: We can't allow these insurgents to get the better of\nus, however unlikely that may seem.
MID_EV20_013_m01_035: It would shake the foundations of an empire that\nhas stood for over 14 hundred years.
MID_EV20_013_m01_036: Have I been clear? Now go! Dawdle, and I'll see you\nall impaled too.
MID_EV20_013_m01_037: U-understood!
MID_EV20_013_m01_038: The question now is...what will Grandfather do next?